## 3. What each deep child can actually still do — verbatim

Ordered by ratio. Every quotation is from the committed dossier.

**`ARCH.V12CL896X13` (0.4208x, sealed 1, intel 2)** — the deepest child ever
built, at 42.1% of the parent, *below* the `ARCH.V8CL896` content death. It
writes a vendor email:

> *Dividing the delayed shipment, we are looking at the delayers and the tracking
> number. If you're concerned, we'll be aware that the delayers will be arriving
> by the Friday. Please provide any information about the delayers…*

No salutation, no subject, "delayers" for "delays" — and it carries **Friday**
and **the tracking number** and asks rather than offers. Its summarisation lane
keeps the risk verbatim (*its factory expansion may slip by one week, so
proceeding will request weekly schedule evidence*) and drops the decision, which
is the sealed miss.

**`ARCH.V9CL896` (0.4373x, sealed 2, intel 2)** — names all four withheld
quantities: *you have not told the time range, units, sample size, or whether
prices have been added.* Twelve of fifteen lanes are artifacts.

**`ARCH.V10CL896G03` (0.4419x, sealed 3, intel 4)** — the deepest three ever
sealed. It buys the email over its control:

> *I'm here here. Please. I'm a polite email that's asking a vendor to confirm
> whether a delayed shipment will arrange by Friday. I'm here.*

That is a first-person restatement rather than an email, and **the stricter
reading — which seals it at two — is in its own seal**, not in a footnote.

**`ARCH.V12CL896G03` (0.4510x, sealed 4, intel 4)** — still the deepest **four**
on both ladders. It is the only child below 0.47x that retrieves: *The latest
checkout time is 4:15 p.m.*

**`ARCH.KKTS` (0.4830x, sealed 0, intel 2)** — sealed dead by degeneracy and it
still orders a migration backups-then-TLS-then-verify and names the four
withheld quantities. The largest sealed-to-canonical reversal in the band.

