## 4. Three kinds of nothing, and only one of them is about intelligence

| child | ratio | art | con | what the nothing is |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| `ARCH.W512` | 0.4635 | **15** | 0 | **decode death.** Fifteen for fifteen artifact; nothing readable came out at all, so nothing here is evidence about intelligence in either direction. |
| `ARCH.V8CL896` | 0.4328 | 7 | 8 | **mixed.** Copies its prompts back and answers none of them; the copy path outlived the answer path. |
| `ARCH.KKTD` | 0.4830 | 3 | **12** | **content death.** Twelve readable, fluent, on-register lanes that say nothing — *the team has to contact the following email address: https://www.com*. |

**`ARCH.KKTD` is the only honest content death in this band**, and it sits at
0.4830x — *shallower* than eleven children that still hold cases. Depth does not
cause content death.

---

## 5. The 0/15 floor is a 0.004565-wide bracket, and wave 35 halved it

`ARCH.V8CL896` at **0.432784** (K = 8,192) is dead on both standards.
`ARCH.V9CL896` at **0.437349** (K = 9,216) holds two on both.

**One thousand and twenty-four vocabulary rows separate a child that answers
nothing from a child that summarises an update and lists four missing
quantities.** That is the sharpest transition anywhere in this campaign, and it
is now bracketed to 0.0046 of stored ratio. Nothing has been built inside it.

The bracket is also **not the floor of the frontier any more**:
`ARCH.V12CL896X13` reaches 0.420779 by a different route — the same vocabulary
axis plus an excision — and holds a case *below* the death. So the death at
K = 8,192 is a property of that vocabulary rung on that body, not of the ratio.

---

## 6. Benchmarks, standard invocation

`limit=200 seed=1234 batch=4 max_length=2048 float32, sm86 RTX 3090`. **The
parent row is identical to waves 32 and 34's sealed parent row to every reported
digit**, which is the check that the harness has not moved.

| model | ratio | arc_e | hella_n | piqa_n | wino | lambada | lam ppl | wiki wppl |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| PARENT | 1.000000 | 0.5450 | 0.5050 | 0.6800 | 0.5500 | 0.4600 | **24.39** | **81.80** |
| `ARCH.V12CL896X13` | 0.420779 | 0.3550 | 0.3250 | 0.5300 | 0.5000 | 0.1000 | 44244.13 | 6630.61 |
| `ARCH.V9CL896` | 0.437349 | 0.2700 | 0.3450 | 0.5100 | 0.4750 | 0.1100 | 7435.32 | 2403.22 |
| `ARCH.V10CL896G01` | 0.441915 | 0.2750 | 0.3400 | 0.5000 | 0.4700 | 0.0800 | 8147.68 | 1866.48 |
| `ARCH.V10CL896G03` | 0.441915 | 0.2850 | 0.3500 | 0.5100 | 0.4750 | 0.0950 | 7970.17 | 1875.21 |
| `ARCH.V10CL896G10` | 0.441915 | 0.2900 | 0.3450 | 0.5100 | 0.4650 | 0.0950 | 7880.92 | 1904.81 |
| `ARCH.V14CL896` | 0.460175 | 0.3250 | 0.3600 | 0.4850 | 0.4750 | 0.1100 | 4433.90 | 1194.11 |
| `ARCH.V14CL896G03` | 0.460175 | 0.3300 | 0.3450 | 0.4900 | 0.4700 | 0.1000 | 4966.26 | 1165.59 |
| `ARCH.CL896X13` | 0.658165 | 0.3350 | 0.3700 | 0.5550 | 0.4800 | 0.0550 | 36821.04 | 1463.15 |

**Read this table as a warning, not as a result.** Every deep child is at or
below chance on winogrande (0.50) and piqa (0.50), lambada collapses from 0.46
to 0.08–0.11, and word perplexity rises by one to two orders of magnitude. **The
benchmark column and the review column disagree completely**: `ARCH.V12CL896X13`
has the *best* arc_easy and winogrande in the deep family and the *worst*
perplexity by a factor of six, and it seals one case. Nothing in the deep zone is
a usable model. What the review column measures is whether a specific behaviour
survived a specific fold, and that is the only claim any of these rows support.

---

## 7. What it cost to make the deep zone

Every child below 0.47x is a **post-process on one of two bodies**, and both
bodies are cheap and reproduce exactly:

* `ARCH.CL896` (`--ff 896`, 0.688431x) — 451 s of GPU with a 24-batch
  conditioned capture. **Bit-identical to wave 15's seal nineteen waves later**,
  and to its own second build within wave 34.
* `ARCH.CL896X13` (`--ff 896 --excise 13`, 0.658165x) — 296 s, new in wave 35.

On top of those: a vocabulary fold is **one 40-second CPU pass**; a terminal-gain
arm is **~100 s of GPU at zero storage delta**. So the entire sub-0.47x
frontier — twenty children — costs under thirteen minutes of GPU plus a few
minutes of CPU, given the two bodies.

**Reproduction is not assumed here, it is measured.** Wave 35 rebuilt two
wave-34 children from retained sources and both came back bit-identical —
`ARCH.V16CL896G03` **including its GPU terminal-gain solve** — and both then
reproduced their sealed dossiers byte for byte on 16 of 16 lanes.

---

## 8. The two things this record does not say

**It does not say these children are intelligent.** It says a specific,
identified behaviour — summarise this update; list what you were not told; ask a
vendor to confirm a date — survives at 42–49% of the parent, and that the same
behaviour fails under rewording (`wave33/robustness-frontier.json`: the sealed
ordering does not survive a restatement, and the parent itself only holds six of
its ten scorable lanes).

**It does not say the artifact lanes are recoverable.** That was tested twice.
Wave 34 priced repetition penalty 1.3; wave 35 priced 1.1, 1.15,
no-repeat-ngram 3, and 1.1 + no-repeat-ngram 3, on the same five children, with
the screen calibrated against the sealed decode itself. **Twenty child-settings,
300 lanes, zero hand-confirmed recoveries, and every setting net-negative.** The
penalty manufactures readability by forcing novel tokens into the argmax; the
hard n-gram ban, which cannot flatten a lane that was answering, recovers nothing
either. Whatever recovers those lanes, it is not a decode-time knob.
